  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I'm gaining weight and I don't know why. I'm eating the same as always, if anything less.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:33",
      "end_timestamp": "00:41",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "How much are we talking about, and over how long?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:43",
      "end_timestamp": "00:48",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "About six kilos, I think? But when did it start... I honestly can't say. Maybe winter, maybe before that.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:50",
      "end_timestamp": "01:00",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Not knowing is fine. Lots of people only notice when their jeans stop doing up. Has anything changed at work or home?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:03",
      "end_timestamp": "01:14",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I work night shifts at the hospital, a few months now. Everything's upside down.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:16",
      "end_timestamp": "01:23",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That can muddle your body clock. Your file says you take a thyroid tablet. Remind me what it's for?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:25",
      "end_timestamp": "01:35",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "For my underactive thyroid. Levothyroxine, 75 micrograms, once a day, every morning before breakfast.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:38",
      "end_timestamp": "01:45",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. And you take it every single day?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:47",
      "end_timestamp": "01:52",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, every morning. Well, most mornings. On night-shift days I honestly can't tell if I've taken it. I worry I've doubled up or missed it.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:55",
      "end_timestamp": "02:07",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "It could. Let me ask about the rest of you. How are your bowels?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:32",
      "end_timestamp": "02:40",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Fine. Regular as clockwork, oddly.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:42",
      "end_timestamp": "02:46",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. Any pounding heart or palpitations, or feeling shaky?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:49",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No palpitations. Nothing like that.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:56",
      "end_timestamp": "03:00",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Okay. Any allergies I should have on file before we go further?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:02",
      "end_timestamp": "03:09",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, actually, that's something I wanted to ask. I'm allergic to penicillin. I came out in hives when I was about twenty.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:10",
      "end_timestamp": "03:22",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Pressure is 124 over 78, pulse 62, and weight 82 kilograms.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:55",
      "end_timestamp": "05:01",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thyroid feels normal in size and smooth. Nothing odd there.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:32",
      "end_timestamp": "05:38",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Nothing I felt points that way. In plain English, I think this is most likely your underactive thyroid not being fully covered, probably because of the patchy doses.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:48",
      "end_timestamp": "06:02",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Not yet. A bigger dose on top of missed ones just makes a rollercoaster. First, lock in the routine. Phone alarm, tablet next to the toothbrush, same time even after a night shift.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:14",
      "end_timestamp": "06:32",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And give it half an hour on its own before your coffee or breakfast.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:40",
      "end_timestamp": "06:48",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    }
